("saint-luke-drawing-the-virgin",7,0,"Saint Luke, who was said to be a painter, kneels to draw Mary as she nurses the baby Jesus, using a metalpoint pen. Rogier van der Weyden painted it in about 1440, and some people think the face of Luke is a self-portrait."),
("saint-sebastian-perugino",7,0,"Saint Sebastian stands tied to a column between two arches with an arrow in his chest, gazing upward calmly. Pietro Perugino painted it in about 1490, and the green landscape behind him is full of soft light."),
