("miracle-of-the-holy-cross-at-the-rialto-bridge",7,0,"A crowd of people in Venice stands on balconies and gondolas around the old wooden Rialto Bridge, where a miracle is happening. Vittore Carpaccio painted it in about 1494, and it shows what the city looked like at the time."),
("portrait-of-francesco-delle-opere",1,0,"A man with long hair and a slight smile stands in front of a window that looks out on a calm landscape. Pietro Perugino painted Francesco delle Opere in 1494, and he was a Florentine craftsman who made fine jewelry."),
("the-epiphany",7,0,"The three kings bring gifts to the baby Jesus, and an odd, strange figure stands in the doorway. Hieronymus Bosch painted it in about 1494, and the mysterious figure has puzzled people ever since."),
("christ-crowned-with-thorns",7,0,"Christ sits in the center of four men who press a crown of thorns on his head, and his eyes stare right at us. Hieronymus Bosch painted it in about 1495, and the men's faces are uglier than anything you would see in real life."),
